      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e @dmaluka@google.com could you provide more details?\n\nLet me just quote myself from the email thread:\n\n\u003e While indeed the upstream discussion suggests that the patch doesn\u0027t\naddress the root cause and thus is rather a workaround, it seems it\nshouldn\u0027t cause harmful side effects (and thus it might be fine to\nmerge it, as long as we absolutely remember to revert it once the\nright fix is ready). What it does is moving a bit of code after\nreleasing the resampler_lock mutex. That mutex is for protecting the\nresampler list, and that moved code doesn\u0027t do anything with that list\nper se.\n\u003e ...\n\u003e BTW also it appears that this issue (i.e. deadlock between multiple\nirqfd_resampler_shutdown instances) affects Pixel, and potentially any\nvendors that use KVM rather than Gunyah or whatever, just as much.\nLooking at https://b.corp.google.com/issues?q\u003dirqfd_resampler_shutdown,\nbesides the last year\u0027s bug b/420528003 already mentioned by Vineeth,\nlooks like it was recently observed on Pixel in multiple other bugs:\nb/493716363, b/485280809, b/485029822",
      "parentUuid": "b999e023_cb79244f",
      "revId": "88297da8c604da5d731df49fc0994c5601ed2587",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
